{"root":{"data":{"id":"dif904ui4qo0","created":1778441801761,"text":"Game Rift"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"dif9859df2w0","created":1778442429573,"text":"CourseTransition","expandState":"expand","layout_right_offset":{"x":-35.99999999999977,"y":-18.666666666666686},"layout":null},"children":[{"data":{"id":"dif8a0qs2hk0","created":1778439755360,"text":"Godot","layout":null,"background":"#7030a0","color":"white"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"dif8abewpnk0","created":1778439778587,"text":"How to Create a 3D Survival Game in Godot 4.2 with GDScript","progress":1,"layout":null,"background":"transparent"},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"dif8acqd6rc0","created":1778439781457,"text":"Blender","layout":null,"expandState":"expand","background":"#7030a0","color":"white"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"dif8ayc3khc0","created":1778439828483,"text":"Blender  Ultimate Game Art Creation Guide","progress":1,"layout":null,"background":"transparent"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"dif8ilthgj40","created":1778440428150,"text":"Blender  Ultimate Game Art Creation Guide","progress":1,"layout":null,"background":"transparent"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"dif8wvcfihs0","created":1778441545985,"text":"Alive! Animation course in Blender","progress":1,"layout":null,"background":"transparent"},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"dif8agzw6sg0","created":1778439790740,"text":"Sounds","layout":null,"background":"#7030a0","color":"white"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"dif8c0d7kbc0","created":1778439911268,"text":"Game Audio Essentials Music Production for Video Games","layout":null,"progress":1,"background":"transparent"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"dif8c6i3c800","created":1778439924624,"text":"Game Audio Essentials SFX & Sound Design For Video Games","progress":1,"layout":null,"background":"transparent"},"children":[]}]}]},{"data":{"id":"dif99h5pa280","created":1778442533837,"text":"GameDev"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"dif9bhshy1s0","created":1778442691944,"text":"Youtube","background":"#92d050"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"difw3jd3tmo0","created":1778506953981,"text":"用 Godot 制作的神级 3D 角色控制器，这将是我们的 ALS！","expandState":"expand","hyperlink":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qIf5YQ8qJng&t=52s","hyperlinkTitle":"atnda","note":"God Tier 3D Character Controller Made In Godot, this will be our ALS!\n\n13,987次观看  2025年6月21日\nYoo!\nThis is the first episode of project Arena's devlog series. In this one I will review the controller core update, and its difference with public controller project. The core idea is, of course, the torso split. Older viewers know that I already have attempted it on the public project, and succeed to some extend, but couldn't call that \"god tier\". However, since then some things changed. Firstly, Godot started to pull its head out of its butt on 3d animation topic and gifted us SkeletonModifier3D technology. With them I power the animation framework flexible enough to pull perfect torso split and 8-directional locomotion blends without loosing my soul to AnimationTree. Secondly, I've got a professional animator that can provide such 8-directional locomotion packages of really nice quality. And finally, the project holds hopes to become commercial one day, so now there are ambitions and money on the line, so I'm sweating.\nI'm quite proud with results, this is a very tranquillizing milestone to me. Of course, I have only a couple examples for how powerful the thing is, but I sat with pen&paper framework, and grew to think I can design the whole titanfall with these bricks. This puts my soul finally at rest, I made The Controller and can now do some other things like enemies, networking or even better animator's utils.\nAgain, there is no project, but I consider this a solid learning material anyways. There are a couple of blurred code pieces in the video, they are not \"privated\" they are hidden to talk about them later down the journey in a couple of minutes. In the end I also include several advice on how to refactor public controller towards this system.\nAlso, some of my videos from the past you might consider useful:\nThis is pretty much the tech I use to animate stuff, minor things changed\n   • Transition to Godot's superior 3d animatio...  \nThese two videos are my previous attempt to torso split, they are a valuable material, but add a grain of salt, nowadays they are a bit morally old, keep in mind this was before we got skelly modifiers:\n   • Godot animation layering pipelines for big...  \n   • Roll dodge, shield block and finite spells...  \nIf somehow you are a new viewer and have no idea what happens, check this one out, I have a 1.25h tutorial series, you are in for a good time:\n   • Use professional AAA practices in your God...  \n\nCheck out our discord, once in a while a wizard appears there and randomly cuts you main frame execution times by half!\n  / discord  \n\nYou can also support the channel on patreon ^_^:\n  / fairfight  \n\nAlso the guy who provides animations makes some awesome 3d tools, check them out!\nhttps://linktr.ee/notthatnda\n\n\n00:00 Why you want to cut your legs\n02:45 Base(d) system\n10:53 Short classes review\n12:42 Final leap to godhood\n14:40 How to refactor public project into this","background":"transparent","progress":2},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"difyce3go280","created":1778513290011,"text":"Godot 4 自定义检查器插件","hyperlink":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xa6YBcrrS7E&t=19s","hyperlinkTitle":"","note":"Custom Inspector Plugins Godot 4\n\n","progress":1},"children":[]}]}]}]},"template":"right","theme":"classic","version":"1.4.43"}